WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 013, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.308
<v Nia>What was lying under the floor of Great House? And why does a census give the farm another name?

2
00:00:11.658 --> 00:00:23.581
<v John Williams>Mary, those Ordnance men are out by the lane again with their chain and brass instrument, measuring every hedge in the parish. Keep the dog in, or he'll have their pegs.

3
00:00:23.931 --> 00:00:40.854
<v Nia>That's 1878. The Ordnance Survey walked Glamorgan for the six-inch map of the Cardiff and Penarth corner, surveyed 1878 to 79 and published in 1885. It's on the National Library of Scotland's site, but nobody has checked yet exactly where Llandough sits on it.

4
00:00:41.204 --> 00:00:51.588
<v Nia>That's sheet forty-seven. The large-scale sheets, forty-seven two to fifteen, do cover Llandough-juxta-Penarth. Glamorgan Archives keeps the council's copies. Fields and buildings, yes. Who owned them, no.

5
00:00:55.938 --> 00:01:07.477
<v Nia>Then, about 1880: armour, reported found under the floor of the rear wing of Great House. It's thought to be the medieval ironwork from Llandough now at the National Museum.

6
00:01:11.827 --> 00:01:26.827
<v Nia>Thought to be. This comes from the Historic Environment Record, a note by Suggett for the Royal Commission in December 1988. It's a record written a century later, not a finder's account, and it names nobody who lifted it.

7
00:01:27.177 --> 00:01:36.023
<v John Williams>Right, the paper for the census man. John Williams, head, fifty-three, farmer. Mary, wife. Then the children, oldest first. Plain and neat, mind.

8
00:01:40.373 --> 00:01:53.450
<v Nia>Census night, the third of April 1881. John Williams, fifty-three, 'Farmer of 170' acres, or maybe 120, the figure's hard to read. His wife Mary and the children. And the address: 'Llandough Home Farm'.

9
00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:06.108
<v Nia>Our case reads that as the census mixing up the Llandough farm with Great House Farm, so it's Great House under another name. That reading sits in the Legal Wiki's Master Timeline.

10
00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:17.612
<v Nia>But be fair to the page. It never writes Great House. It shows a John Williams, a Mary, and a farm on census night. The rest is our reading.
